// MOTS Supplier Portal - validation message catalogue (API-ARCHITECTURE.md §7.2)
//
// THIS FILE IS THE REVIEWABLE ARTEFACT. Every Arabic and English sentence the API can return for a
// field-level validation failure is here, and nowhere else; the code reads this file rather than
// carrying strings of its own. It is meant to be read end to end without opening any C#.
//
// One entry per (field, rule) pair. There are 92, matching the 92 pairs the validators declare -
// ValidationCatalogueCoverageTests fails the build in BOTH directions: a rule with no entry here,
// and an entry here for a rule that no longer exists.
//
//   "source": "§7.2"     transcribed verbatim from the API contract's worked exemplars
//              "SPA"     reused verbatim from Arabic already shipping in the SPA (i18n/config.ts)
//              "drafted" written for this catalogue and NOT YET APPROVED - read these hardest
//
//   "flag"    present only where the drafting involved a judgement call. One line saying which.
//
// On the Arabic. UX-WRITING.md §1.3 requires native authoring in professional MSA, not translation
// of the English. Predicates agree with their subject's gender - «العنوان مطلوب» but «المدينة
// مطلوبة» - which is why §9's fixed {field} patterns were not usable and each sentence is written
// out. Numerals are Arabic-Indic, matching dates, counts and quantities in the SPA.

[

  // ========================================================================================
  // Identity, access and invitations
  // Login, password reset, MFA, and the two invite-acceptance flows (staff and supplier user).
  // ========================================================================================
  {
    "key": "Email.NotEmpty",
